  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5601.02 Certificate of authority",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5601.02 \"Certificate of authority\" means a letter issued by a person who is authorized to obtain motor vehicle record information, appointing an agent to act on his/her behalf for a specific purpose allowed by RSA 260:14 and a specific time period.\n\nSource. #7361, EXEMPT, eff 9-1-00; ss by #7621, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-02",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5600.html"
